+Optical Character Recognition (OCR) is the process of extracting text from images.
+Single-line images can be processed directly.
+For document images, a segmentation file in
+[ALTO](https://www.loc.gov/standards/alto/) or
+[PAGE XML](https://github.com/PRImA-Research-Lab/PAGE-XML/wiki) format is required.
+This additional input file can be produced by the Kraken segmentation tool,
 which is also available in the Kraken OCR suite.
 
-The OCR output can be returned in various formats, 
-including [ALTO](https://www.loc.gov/standards/alto/), 
-[PageXML](https://github.com/PRImA-Research-Lab/PAGE-XML/wiki), 
-[hOCR](https://kba.github.io/hocr-spec/1.2/), 
-[abbyyXML](https://support.abbyy.com/hc/en-us/articles/360017270080-Output-XML-document), and plain text.
+The OCR process requires a pre-trained model. You can either upload your own model in
+[mlmodel](https://apple.github.io/coremltools/mlmodel/index.html) or
+[safetensors](https://huggingface.co/docs/safetensors/index) format,
+or select a model available on the Galaxy instance.
+For model metadata, such as covered languages, scripts, and license information,
+consult Zenodo or [Kraken's model catalog](https://htrmopo.inria.fr).
+Please remember to cite the model you use.
+
+The OCR output can be returned in various formats,
+including [ALTO](https://www.loc.gov/standards/alto/),
+[PageXML](https://github.com/PRImA-Research-Lab/PAGE-XML/wiki),
+[hOCR](https://kba.github.io/hocr-spec/1.2/),
+[abbyyXML](https://support.abbyy.com/hc/en-us/articles/360017270080-Output-XML-document),
+and plain text.
 
 **License**
 
 Kraken is licensed under the Apache-2.0 license.
+]]>
